Subject: [overlay 0019] Key_GetBindingForKey — per-key binding lookup for the shell

The shell must apply the rerelease default GAMEPAD layout to pad keys nothing has
bound (a vanilla-pak install execs a 1997 default.cfg with no pad section — every
pad button dead while the hardwired analog sticks work: the 2026-07-12 Vision Pro
report). Binding through the console `bind` command would clobber user rebinds, so
the shell needs to read a single key's live binding; keybindings[] is file-static
and Key_GetBinding() is the reverse (binding->key) lookup. patch -p1 -d vendor/q2repro

--- a/inc/client/keys.h
+++ b/inc/client/keys.h
@@ -167,3 +167,4 @@
 
 void    Key_WaitKey(keywaitcb_t wait, void *arg);
 bool    Key_IsWaiting(void);   // [iOS overlay] pad-rebind capture state
+const char *Key_GetBindingForKey(int keynum);   // [iOS overlay] "" when unbound
--- a/src/client/keys.c
+++ b/src/client/keys.c
@@ -925,4 +925,14 @@
 bool Key_IsWaiting(void)
 {
     return key_wait_cb != NULL;
+}
+
+// [iOS overlay] Binding text for one key ("" when unbound). Lets the shell apply the
+// rerelease default GAMEPAD layout only to keys nothing has bound — a vanilla-pak
+// install execs a 1997 default.cfg with no pad section, leaving every pad key dead.
+const char *Key_GetBindingForKey(int keynum)
+{
+    if (keynum < 0 || keynum > 255 || !keybindings[keynum])
+        return "";
+    return keybindings[keynum];
 }
